        <owl:annotatedTarget xml:lang="en">sternum</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:AISM_0000171 xml:lang="en">Beutel RG, Friedrich F, Yang X-K, Ge S-Q (2014) Insect Morphology and Phylogeny Insect morphology and phylogeny: a textbook for students of entomology. De Gruyter.

https://doi.org/10.1515/9783110264043

&quot;Sternum: ventral wall of thoracic (or abdominal) segment, usually divided into presternum, basisternum, furcasternum and spinasternum in unspecialized hexapods; largely or completely invaginated in Holometabola (cryptosterny).&quot;</obo:AISM_0000171>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


