        <obo:IAO_0000115>A flattened, almost circular bilaminar plate of cells formed when the inner cell mass (aka embryoblast) forms two epithelial layers, each of a distinct lineage, separated by an extracellular basement membrane: the external (dorsal) layer is called the epiblast and the internal (ventral) layer is called the hypoblast (aka primitive endoderm); together, they compose the bilaminar embryonic disc.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboI:hasDbXref>FMA:293863</oboI:hasDbXref>
        <oboI:hasDbXref>NCIT:C34112</oboI:hasDbXref>
        <oboI:hasDbXref>UMLS:C1283997</oboI:hasDbXref>
        <oboI:hasDbXref>Wikipedia:Bilaminar_disc</oboI:hasDbXref>
        <oboI:hasExactSynonym>bilaminary embryonic disc</oboI:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboI:hasExactSynonym>bilaminary germ disc</oboI:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboI:hasOBONamespace>uberon</oboI:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboI:id>UBERON:0000091</oboI:id>
        <rdfs:label>bilaminar disc</rdfs:label>
        <x_0.1:depiction rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI">http://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e3/Gray21.png</x_0.1:depiction>
    </owl:Class>
