            </owl:Restriction>
        </owl:disjointWith>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Somites are spheres of epithelial cells that form sequentially along the anterior-posterior axis of the embryo through mesenchymal to epithelial transition of the presomitic mesoderm.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000232>EDITOR_NOTE currently classified as an epithelial vesicle, consistent with EHDAA2 and https://github.com/obophenotype/uberon/wiki/The-neural-crest. Consider making &apos;somitic mesoderm&apos; a separate term and correlate with regionalization processes. Consider moving ZFA term to &apos;trunk somite&apos; as it is part of the trunk</obo:IAO_0000232>
        <oboI:hasDbXref>AAO:0010569</oboI:hasDbXref>
        <oboI:hasDbXref>AEO:0001015</oboI:hasDbXref>
